{
  "id": "u06-l04",
  "unit": "u06-bazaar",
  "title": "This one, those ones",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**এই** (*ei*) 'this' and **ওই** (*oi*) 'that' go before a noun: **এই দোকানদার** 'this shopkeeper'. On their own, add **-টা**: **এইটা** 'this one', **ওইটা** 'that one' (spoken forms of the এটা / ওটা you know).\n\n**-টা** on a noun makes it specific, like 'the': **মাছটা** 'the fish'. **-গুলো** makes it specific *and* plural: **কলাগুলো** 'the bananas'.\n\n- **এইটা / এটা** — this one\n- **ওইটা / ওটা** — that one\n- **এগুলো** — these\n- **ওগুলো** — those\n\nYou'll often hear both together: **এই মাছটা** 'this fish'. That's normal.\n\n'Not this one, that one' is **এইটা না, ওইটা।** If nothing looks good, ask for **অন্য একটা** 'a different one'. Picking your own fish or fruit is normal; vendors expect you to point.",
  "vocab": [
    {
